    "background_story": "Julius was a seasoned proctor with a keen eye for detail. For years, he had been responsible for invigilating high-stakes exams at the prestigious St. Michael's Academy. His no-nonsense demeanor and sharp instincts made him a master at detecting even the slightest hint of cheating. Julius took his job very seriously, knowing that the integrity of the exams was paramount. He would often arrive hours before the exams to ensure that every detail, from the seating arrangements to the distribution of materials, was meticulously in place. His eagle eye and quick reflexes had foiled many a would-be cheater, earning him the respect and admiration of students and faculty alike. Julius's dedication to fair play and academic integrity made him an unsung hero of the academic world.",
